.TH "waybar\-hyprland\-workspaces" "5" "2026\-08\-07"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- hyprland workspaces module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBworkspaces\fR module displays the currently used workspaces in hyprland compositor.\&
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Addressed by \fBhyprland/workspaces\fR
.PP
\fBformat\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: {name} 
.br
The format, how information should be displayed.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-icons\fR: 
.br
typeof: object 
.br
Based on the workspace ID and state, the corresponding icon gets selected.\& See \fBicons\fR.\&
.PP
\fBwindow\-rewrite\fR: 
.br
typeof: object 
.br
Regex rules to map window class to an icon or preferred method of representation for a workspace'\&s window.\&
.RS 4
Keys are the rules, while the values are the methods of representation.\& Values may use the placeholders {class} and {title} to use the window'\&s original class and/or title respectively.\&
Rules may specify `class<.\&.\&.\&>`, `title<.\&.\&.\&>`, or both in order to fine\-tune the matching.\&
You may assign an empty value to a rule to have it ignored from generating any representation in workspaces.\& 
.br
This setting is ignored if \fBworkspace\-taskbar.\&enable\fR is set to true.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBwindow\-rewrite\-default\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: "?\&" 
.br
The default method of representation for a workspace'\&s window.\& This will be used for windows whose classes do not match any of the rules in \fBwindow\-rewrite\fR.\& 
.br
This setting is ignored if \fBworkspace\-taskbar.\&enable\fR is set to true.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-window\-separator\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: " " 
.br
The separator to be used between windows in a workspace.\& 
.br
This setting is ignored if \fBworkspace\-taskbar.\&enable\fR is set to true.\&
.PP
\fBwindow\-rewrite\-group\-threshold\fR: 
.br
typeof: int 
.br
default: 0 
.br
When a workspace contains at least this many windows with the same rewrite result, they are collapsed into a single one using \fBwindow\-rewrite\-group\-format\fR.\& 
.br
Set to 0 to disable grouping.\& 
.br
This setting is ignored if \fBworkspace\-taskbar.\&enable\fR is set to true.\&
.PP
\fBwindow\-rewrite\-group\-format\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: "{icon}×{count}" 
.br
The format used to represent a group of collapsed windows.\& Available placeholders are {icon} (the icon being grouped) and {count} (how many windows share it).\& 
.br
This setting is ignored if \fBworkspace\-taskbar.\&enable\fR is set to true.\&
.PP
\fBworkspace\-taskbar\fR: 
.br
typeof: object 
.br
Contains settings for the workspace taskbar, an alternative mode for the workspaces module which displays the window icons as images instead of text.\&
.RS 4
.PP
.RS 4
\fBenable\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables the workspace taskbar mode.\&
.PP
\fBupdate\-active\-window\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If true, the active/focused window will have an '\&active'\& class.\& Could cause higher CPU usage due to more frequent redraws.\&
.PP
\fBreverse\-direction\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If true, the taskbar windows will be added in reverse order (right to left if orientation is horizontal, bottom to top if vertical).\&
.PP
\fBactive\-window\-position\fR: 
.br
typeof: "none" | "first" | "last" 
.br
default: "none" 
.br
If set to "first", the active window will be moved at the beginning of the taskbar.\& If set to "last", it will be moved at the end.\& It will only work if \fBupdate\-active\-window\fR is set to true.\&
.PP
\fBformat\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: {icon} 
.br
Format to use for each window in the workspace taskbar.\& Available placeholders are {icon} and {title}.\&
.PP
\fBicon\-size\fR: 
.br
typeof: int 
.br
default: 16 
.br
Size of the icons in the workspace taskbar.\&
.PP
\fBmax\-icons\fR: 
.br
typeof: int 
.br
default: 0 (unlimited) 
.br
Maximum number of icons to show per workspace.\& When set, duplicate icons (windows with the same class) are removed first, then the list is trimmed to this limit.\& Set to 0 for unlimited icons.\&
.PP
\fBicon\-theme\fR: 
.br
typeof: string | array 
.br
default: [] 
.br
Icon theme to use for the workspace taskbar.\& If an array is provided, the first theme that is found for a given icon will be used.\& If no theme is found (or the array is empty), the default icon theme is used.\&
.PP
\fBorientation\fR: 
.br
typeof: "horizontal" | "vertical" 
.br
default: horizontal 
.br
Direction in which the workspace taskbar is displayed.\&
.PP
\fBignore\-list\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
default: [] 
.br
Regex patterns to match against window class or window title.\& If a window'\&s class OR title matches any of the patterns, it will not be shown.\&
.PP
\fBon\-click\-window\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: "" 
.br
Command to run when a window is clicked.\& Available placeholders are: 
.br
\- {address} Hyprland address of the clicked window.\& 
.br
\- {button} Pressed button number, see https://api.\&gtkd.\&org/gdk.\&c.\&types.\&GdkEventButton.\&button.\&html.\& 
.br
See https://github.\&com/Alexays/Waybar/wiki/Module:\-Hyprland#workspace\-taskbars\-example for a full example.\&
.PP
.RE
.RE
\fBmax\-windows\fR: 
.br
typeof: int 
.br
default: 0 (unlimited) 
.br
Maximum number of windows to show per workspace.\& When set, newest windows beyond the limit are not shown.\& Set to 0 for unlimited windows.\&
.PP
\fBshow\-special\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to true, special workspaces will be shown.\&
.PP
\fBspecial\-visible\-only\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If this and show\-special are to true, special workspaces will be shown only if visible.\&
.PP
\fBpersistent\-only\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to true, only persistent workspaces will be shown on bar.\&
.PP
\fBpersistent\-workspaces\fR: 
.br
typeof: object 
.br
default: empty 
.br
Lists workspaces that should always be shown, even when they do not exist.\& Keys are workspace names and values are arrays of output names on which the workspace should be shown (an empty array means all outputs).\& See the examples below.\& 
.br
Note: for persistent workspaces to actually work you must also declare them in your Hyprland config, e.\&g.\& \fBworkspace = 1, monitor:eDP\-1, persistent:true\fR.\&
.PP
\fBall\-outputs\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to false workspaces group will be shown only in assigned output.\& Otherwise, all workspace groups are shown.\&
.PP
\fBactive\-only\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to true, only the active workspace will be shown.\&
.PP
\fBhide\-active\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to true, the active workspace will be hidden.\& Unless a workspace is persistent or special.\&
.PP
\fBmove\-to\-monitor\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to true, open the workspace on the current monitor when clicking on a workspace button.\&
.RS 4
Otherwise, the workspace will open on the monitor where it was previously assigned.\&
Analog to using `focusworkspaceoncurrentmonitor` dispatcher instead of `workspace` in Hyprland.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBunique\-icons\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to true, only one instance of each window icon will be shown per workspace.\&
.PP
\fBenable\-bar\-scroll\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
If set to false, you can'\&t scroll to cycle throughout workspaces from the entire bar.\& If set to true this behaviour is enabled.\&
.PP
\fBon\-scroll\-up\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Command to execute when scrolling up on the module.\& This replaces the default behaviour of workspace cycling.\&
.PP
\fBon\-scroll\-down\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
Command to execute when scrolling down on the module.\& This replaces the default behaviour of workspace cycling.\&
.PP
\fBignore\-workspaces\fR: 
.br
typeof: array 
.br
default: [] 
.br
Regexes to match against workspaces names.\& If there'\&s a match, the workspace will not be shown.\& This takes precedence over \fBshow\-special\fR, \fBall\-outputs\fR, and \fBactive\-only\fR.\&
.PP
\fBsort\-by\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: "default" 
.br
If set to number, workspaces will sort by number.\&
.RS 4
If set to name, workspaces will sort by name.\&
If set to id, workspaces will sort by id.\&
If set to special\-centered, workspaces will sort by default with special workspaces in the center.\&
If none of those, workspaces will sort with default behavior.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBtooltip\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: true 
.br
Option to disable tooltip on hover.\&
.PP
\fBtooltips\fR: 
.br
typeof: object 
.br
Based on the workspace ID and state, the corresponding tooltip gets selected.\& Selection works the same as \fBformat\-icons\fR do.\& Format replacements are supported.\& See \fBicons\fR.\&
.PP
\fBexpand\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables this module to consume all left over space dynamically.\&
.PP
.SH FORMAT REPLACEMENTS
.PP
\fB{id}\fR: id of workspace assigned by compositor
.PP
\fB{name}\fR: workspace name assigned by compositor
.PP
\fB{icon}\fR: Icon, as defined in \fBformat\-icons\fR.\&
.PP
\fB{windows}\fR: The windows in the workspace, formatted according to \fBwindow\-rewrite\fR and joined with \fBformat\-window\-separator\fR.\&
.PP
.SH WINDOW REWRITE RULES
.PP
The rules in \fBwindow\-rewrite\fR are regexes that may match against a window'\&s
class, title, or both.\& There are four categories of rule, distinguished by how
they are written in the config:
.PP
.TS
allbox;c c
l l
l l
l l
l l.
T{
\fBRule\fR
T}	T{
\fBCategory\fR
T}
T{
\fBsomething\fR
T}	T{
Vague
T}
T{
\fBclass<something>\fR
T}	T{
Class\-only
T}
T{
\fBtitle<something>\fR
T}	T{
Title\-only
T}
T{
\fBclass<something1> title<something2>\fR
T}	T{
Hybrid
T}
.TE
.sp 1
When the config contains only "vague" rules, they are matched against window
\fBclasses\fR only.\& This is both for backwards compatibility and for performance:
matching against the title requires listening to window title changes via
Hyprland'\&s IPC, which is unnecessary when no title rule is in use.\&
.PP
When the config contains \fBat least one\fR "title\-only" or "hybrid" rule, then all
"vague" rules match against \fBboth\fR class and title.\& This lets you define vague
rules where it does not matter whether the class or the title matched.\&
.PP
.SH ICONS
.PP
Additional to workspace name matching, the following \fBformat\-icons\fR can be set.\&
.PP
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBdefault\fR: Will be shown, when no string match is found and none of the below conditions have defined icons.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBactive\fR: Will be shown, when workspace is active
.IP \(bu 4
\fBspecial\fR: Will be shown on non\-active special workspaces
.IP \(bu 4
\fBempty\fR: Will be shown on non\-active, non\-special empty persistent workspaces
.IP \(bu 4
\fBvisible\fR: Will be shown on workspaces that are visible but not active.\& For example: this is useful if you want your visible workspaces on other monitors to have the same look as active.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBpersistent\fR: Will be shown on non\-empty persistent workspaces
.IP \(bu 4
\fBurgent\fR: Will be shown on non\-active urgent workspaces
.PD
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"hyprland/workspaces": {
	"format": "{name}: {icon}",
	"format\-icons": {
		"1": "",
		"2": "",
		"3": "",
		"4": "",
		"5": "",
		"active": "",
		"default": ""
	},
	"persistent\-workspaces": {
		"*": 5, // 5 workspaces by default on every monitor
		"HDMI\-A\-1": 3 // but only three on HDMI\-A\-1
	}
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
